    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0240" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853B.20/48: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-07T22:00:00+01:00">April 7, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 7—9:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>295. Department’s telegrams 319, March 31, 9 p.m. and 326, April 1, 2 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">10</hi>] p.m. I at once sent notes to the Foreign
                    Minister in the sense of those telegraphic instructions and requested an
                    appointment with Sampayo<anchor n="20" xml:id="d199-f1"/> in order to take up
                    matter orally. He had left for the country to be gone over Good Friday and
                    Easter. I have repeated my request but the Foreign Office has not yet fixed an
                    appointment.</p>
                <p>The British inform me they have sent to the Foreign Office a note along the lines
                    of the Department’s telegram No. 319.</p>
                <p>I shall not fail to telegraph further as soon as I have seen the Secretary
                    General.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d199-f1" n="20" xml:id="d199-f1-content">
                <p>Teixeira de Sampayo, Portuguese Secretary General for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
